From: Uwe Augustin <Info@FlapsOnline.de>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:53:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] OpenVarioSystemWidget: count the rows without the
 upgrade button

When the firmware row took over the upgrade, the button below it went
away, but the row indices still counted it.  Save() therefore read the
"Start after boot" choice from the row of the calibration button: a
debug build stops at the assertion in RowFormWidget, a release build
on the OpenVario crashed with a segmentation fault (exit code 139) as
soon as the configuration dialog was closed.
---
 src/Dialogs/Settings/Panels/OpenVarioSystemWidget.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Dialogs/Settings/Panels/OpenVarioSystemWidget.cpp b/src/Dialogs/Settings/Panels/OpenVarioSystemWidget.cpp
index cd159dcbb..2dc4a5251 100644
--- a/src/Dialogs/Settings/Panels/OpenVarioSystemWidget.cpp
+++ b/src/Dialogs/Settings/Panels/OpenVarioSystemWidget.cpp
@@ -29,9 +29,10 @@
 #include <string>
 #include <string_view>
 
+/* the order of the rows Prepare() adds; the firmware row starts the
+   upgrade itself, there is no button of its own any more */
 enum ControlIndex {
   IMAGE,
-  UPGRADE,
   MAIN_APP,
   CALIBRATE_SENSORS,
   SYSTEM_BACKUP,
